wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(9845613147606718020)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(9845611008084535561)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>1
,p_display_sequence=>10
,p_static_id=>'attribute_01'
,p_prompt=>'Dialog ID'
,p_attribute_type=>'TEXT'
,p_is_required=>true
,p_display_length=>30
,p_max_length=>128
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_examples=>'myCustomPopupDialog'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter the Static ID of the inline modal dialog region that will open to choose a value for this item. The dialog widget must have getValue and setValue methods. It must also set the dialog option "valueConfirmed" to true when a value has been sele'
||'cted and accepted by the user. For example when an OK button is pressed.</p>',
'<p>Here is an example of code that adds getValue and setValue methods:</p>',
'',
'<pre><code>var inst = $("#myCustomPopupDialog").data("ui-dialog");',
'inst.dialogValue = "";',
'inst.setValue = function(value) {',
'    this.dialogValue = value;',
'};',
'inst.getValue = function() {',
'    return this.dialogValue;',
'};',
'</code></pre>',
'',
'<p>This code needs to run when the page loads. In this example the value is stored as a property of the widget instance. You could also put the value in a page item in the dialog region.</p>',
'',
'<p>To set the <code>valueConfirmed</code> option use code like this:</p>',
'<pre><code>$("#myCustomPopupDialog").dialog("option", "valueConfirmed", true);',
'</code></pre>'))
);
