begin
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page(
 p_id=>5
,p_name=>'Dynamic Column Total'
,p_step_title=>'Dynamic Column Total'
,p_autocomplete_on_off=>'OFF'
,p_javascript_code=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'// create a private scope where $ is set to apex.jQuery',
'(function($) {',
'    // This is the function that calculates over all the rows of the model and then',
'    // updates something else.',
'    // Change this to do whatever calculation is needed.',
'    // Call this whenever the model data changes.',
'    function update(model) {',
'        var salKey = model.getFieldKey("SAL"), ',
'            total = 0;',
'',
'        console.log(">> starting sum SAL column")',
'        model.forEach(function(record, index, id) {',
'            var sal = parseFloat(record[salKey]),  // record[salKey] should be a little faster than using model.getValue in a loop',
'                meta = model.getRecordMetadata(id);',
'',
'            if (!isNaN(sal) && !meta.deleted && !meta.agg) {',
'                total += sal;',
'            }',
'        });',
'        console.log(">> setting sum SAL column to " + total)',
'        $s("P5_TOTAL", total);',
'    }',
'',
'    //',
'    // This is the general pattern for subscribing to model notifications',
'    //',
'',
'    // need to do this here rather than in Execute when Page Loads so that the handler',
'    // is setup BEFORE the IG is initialized otherwise miss the first model created event',
'    $(function() {',
'        // the model gets released and created at various times such as when the report changes',
'        // listen for model created events so that we can subscribe to model notifications',
'        $("#emp").on("interactivegridviewmodelcreate", function(event, ui) {',
'            var sid,',
'                model = ui.model;',
'',
'            // note this is only done for the grid veiw. It could be done for',
'            // other views if desired. The imporant thing to realize is that each',
'            // view has its own model',
'            if ( ui.viewId === "grid" ) {',
'                sid = model.subscribe( {',
'                    onChange: function(type, change) {',
'                        console.log(">> model changed ", type, change);',
'                        if ( type === "set" ) {',
'                            // don''t bother to recalculate if other columns change',
'                            if (change.field === "SAL" ) {',
'                                update( model );',
'                            }',
'                        } else if (type !== "move" && type !== "metaChange") {',
'                            // any other change except for move and metaChange affect the calculation',
'                            update( model );',
'                        }',
'                    },',
'                    progressView: $("#P5_TOTAL") // this will cause a spinner on this field',
'                } );',
'                // if not lazy loaded there is no notification for initial data so update',
'                update( model ); ',
'                // just in case fetch all the data. Model notifications will',
'                // cause calls to update so nothing to do in the callback function.',
'                // can remove if data will always be less than 50 records',
'                model.fetchAll(function() {});',
'            }',
'        });',
'',
'    });',
'',
'})(apex.jQuery);',
''))
,p_page_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_page_component_map=>'21'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(36669777653138376260)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>This page demonstrates calculating a value from all the data in the client side data model.',
'A few people have wanted to process the whole data model on the client. ',
'For example calculating the total of a column and keeping it in sync as the grid is edited. ',
'See <a href=''https://community.oracle.com/thread/4003463'' target=''_blank''>here</a>,',
'<a href=''https://community.oracle.com/thread/4005143'' target=''_blank''>here</a> and',
'<a href=''https://community.oracle.com/message/14174982'' target=''_blank''>here</a>',
'</p>',
'<p>The assumption is that the model is going to contain all the data. There are',
'many uses cases where the amount of data is of a resonable size. Care must be ',
'taken that too much data isn''t loaded on the client.',
'Currently the server sends only 50 records initially (if Lazy Loading is No). ',
'The client fetches more data as needed; currently 100 records at a time by default.',
'The model fetchAll method is used to ensure that the model contains all the data.',
'This code can be removed if you are sure the number of records is always less',
'than 50.',
'</p>',
'<p>Client side calcualations should be advisory only. ',
'The server should validate or redo all calculations. Fields updated should probably have',
'warn on unsaved changes set to ignore or perhaps they are display/read only.',
'There is an extra insert model notification due to auto add row when the report changes. To ',
'avoid this set Add Row If Empty to No.</p>',
'<p>This page demonstrates the correct method of getting access to the model and',
'subscribing to model notifications. Once you get access to the model, looping',
'and doing the calculation is easy. The problem is that the model itself is destroyed',
'and created over time. Also there are many changes that can affect the calculation.',
'That is why a model notification listener is subscribed so that the calculation',
'can be redone when needed. In this example the calculation is only done',
'for the grid view model so a viewchange notification is used to hide the total',
'when the grid view is not the current view. A jQuery selector is used rather than a region',
'because specifying an IG region changes the definition of Fire on Initialization',
'to be when a row is edited and here we want page load.',
'</p>',
'<p>Demonstrates:<br>',
'Loading all the data (use with caution), Looping over the data to calculate a value.',
'Handling the custom viewchange event.',
'<br>Customizations:<br>',
'See Page attribute JavaScript: Function and Global Variable Declaration.',
'Dynamic Action view change. Play around with pagination settings, view',
'definitions, lazy loading, and saved Reports.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'Seems like a viewchange event on the IG region should have Fire on Initialization',
'apply to page load not row edit.',
'</p>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
