wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35807068277965641665)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>This page shows how to edit IG records in a dialog using the undocumented $.apex.recordView.createModelEditDialog function.',
'This is the same thing that is used to implement all the IG dialogs such as Filters and Sort.',
'The beneift is a familar editing pattern but without having to create a separate',
'APEX modal page and the associated performance overhead of making extra requests',
'to to fetch record data and refresh the grid after every row edit. There',
'is no need to request more data from the server because it is already in the model.',
'</p>',
'<p>The IG is editable so the model is editable but the grid view is configured',
'to not allow the user to enter edit mode. The toolbar Edit button is removed.',
'The row actions menu is replaced with buttons. The Add Row action is modified',
'so that it opens the same dialog as the new row edit action.',
'</p>',
'<p>Customizations:<br>',
'Code to create the dialog is in Function and Global Variable Declaration.',
'See inline CSS for grid style fixes and for hiding/showing action buttons.',
'IG Advanced JavaScript Code has toolbar customization and add/update actions.',
'<br>Update for V6: Now includes code to make cascading LOV items and DA actions that',
'use PL/SQL work. Also shows how the recordView field layout can be customized and controled.',
'<br>Issues:</br>',
'Would be nice if it were easier to turn off edit mode in grid.<br>',
'Would be nice if there were a simple way to enable or disable the delete button depending on if the row can be deleted.<br>',
'Consider exposing a way to hook into IG _updateActions so custom actions state can be updated as IG state changes.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
