,p_name=>'Always Edit'
,p_step_title=>'Always Edit'
,p_first_item=>'AUTO_FIRST_ITEM'
,p_autocomplete_on_off=>'OFF'
,p_javascript_code=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'// create a private scope where $ is set to apex.jQuery',
'(function($) {',
'',
'    // do this after the page loads but before the IG is initialized to catch the initial events',
'    $(function() {',
'        //',
'        // This is the general pattern for doing something to the view each time it is created',
'        //',
'        // listen for view change events to find out when grid views are created ',
'        $("#emp").on("interactivegridviewchange", function(event, data) {',
'            if ( data.view === "grid" && data.created ) {',
'                // as soon as the grid view is created go into edit mode',
'                // but actually need a little delay THINK why is this?',
'                setTimeout(function() {',
'                    var ig$ = apex.region("emp").widget();',
'                    ig$.interactiveGrid("getActions").set("edit", true);',
'                    // if the user tries to leave edit mode with Escape key return to edit mode',
'                    var grid$ = ig$.interactiveGrid("getViews").grid.view$;',
'                    grid$.on("gridmodechange", function(event, ui) {',
'                        if ( !ui.editMode ) {',
'                            // just setting the edit mode back to true isn''t enough (perhaps it should be).',
'                            // there is an issue with the cell not being reactivated',
'                            // so simulate a double click to go back into edit mode',
'                            setTimeout(function() {',
'                                if ( grid$.find(".a-GV-cell.is-focused").trigger("dblclick").length === 0) {',
'                                    // but if no cell is focused (could have left edit mode because of api call)',
'                                    // just go back into edit mode',
'                                    ig$.interactiveGrid("getActions").set("edit", true);',
'                                }',
'                            }, 100);',
'                        }',
'                    });',
'                }, 1);',
'            }',
'        });',
'',
'    });',
'})(apex.jQuery);',
''))
,p_page_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_page_component_map=>'21'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(36223314695426052885)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>A big difference between IG and Tabular forms from a user perspective is that ',
'IG has distinct navigation and editing modes. This is mainly done for accessiblity',
'and usability reasons. Related to this is that IG only shows the editable component',
'in the focused cell. As you move from cell to cell in edit mode only the focused',
'cell shows an edit control all the other cells show the static display text.',
'This was done for performance and scalability.</p>',
'',
'<p>In use cases where there are always just a few rows and columns some people have wanted',
'the tabular form style where controls are shown in every cell all the time. If you',
'need this then a tabular form is the way to go; IG can''t do it and I don''t think it',
'ever will. A potential half way point may be to always have the IG in edit mode.</p>',
'',
'<p>Demonstrates:<br>',
'Putting the IG in edit mode and when the user tries to leave edit mode setting',
'the IG back to edit mode. Removing the Edit button from the toolbar.',
'<br>Customizations:<br>',
'See the code in page attribute Function and Global Variable Declaration. ',
'(Note: Prior to 19.2 multiple selection doesn''t work well in edit mode so turn it off.)',
'See IG Advanced JavaScript for the code to remove the Edit button and attempt',
'to deal with Single Row View.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'Would be nice if the dubble click hack to put the IG back into edit mode wasn''t needed.<br>',
'Perhaps the grid widget should have an alwaysEdit option like recordView widget (SRV).<br>',
'Perhaps the grid widget should have an option to show all the controls in the current row.<br>',
'For single selection the selection actions menu is not that useful.<br>',
'There is an issue with single row view. It allows the user to leave edit mode. Trying',
'to solve this by forcing SRV into edit mode runs in to a bug when changing reports.',
'The solution used here is to remove single row view. See comments for details.<br>',
'A problem with always being in edit mode is that cell range selection doesn''t work.',
'</p>',
'',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
