,p_step_title=>'Wide Report'
,p_autocomplete_on_off=>'OFF'
,p_javascript_code_onload=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'function resizeMainContent() {',
'    var height = $(window).height(); // start with the window height',
'    // subtract off all the fixed height regions and header',
'    height -= $("#notes").outerHeight();',
'    height -= $(".t-Header").outerHeight();',
'    height -= $("#t_Body_content_offset").height();',
'    height -= $(".t-Footer").outerHeight();',
'    height -= $("#emp .t-Region-header").outerHeight();',
'    height -= 2; // - 2 for the border on the IG region',
'    // if the screen is very small then the responsive features of UT kick in',
'    // and the height set on the notes region for example gets ignored. ',
'    // So just incase set a minimum height for the report',
'    if ( height < 200 ) {',
'        height = 200;',
'    }',
'    // then set the height of the regions that will stretch',
'    // setOuterHeight takes into consideration the borders etc. on the grid itself.',
'    apex.util.setOuterHeight(apex.region("emp").widget(), height);',
'}',
'$(window).on("apexwindowresized", resizeMainContent);',
'resizeMainContent();'))
,p_css_file_urls=>'#IMAGE_PREFIX#plugins/com.oracle.apex.starrating_modern/com_oracle_apex_starrating_modern.css'
,p_inline_css=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'/* If trying to maximize the screen space available for the wide grid region',
' * you may not want much or any padding on the main body.',
' */',
'.t-Body-contentInner {',
'    padding: 0;',
'}',
'/* The region heights will be set in JavaScript so don''t want the body to ',
' * have an explicit height */',
'.t-Body-content {',
'    min-height: initial;',
'}',
'/* If the main page never scrolls then there is little point in a back to top button',
' * You could hide the while footer (.t-Footer) but at that point you may want',
' * to look at creating a custom page template such as ''Fit to Window'' that doesn''t have a footer.',
' */',
'.t-Footer-top {',
'    display: none;',
'}',
''))
,p_step_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108645694512181358)
,p_page_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_page_component_map=>'21'
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(32331336321360983307)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_name=>'notes'
,p_region_css_classes=>'i-h140'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--scrollBody:margin-bottom-none'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108658789039181378)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>When a report contains a large number of columns and rows it can lead to a ',
'usability issue because you must first scroll vertically to the bottom of the ',
'report to get to the horizontal scrollbar. There are many forum questions',
'about this. For example <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/thread/4172637">this</a>',
'and <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/thread/4166983">this</a>.',
'It is often blamed on Interactive Grid and some people have requested that',
'the IG horizontal scrollbar stick to the bottom of the page.',
'The issue is not specific to Interactive Grid and has come up in relation to',
'Interactive Report for example <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/message/13362035">here</a>',
'and <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/message/13782816">here</a>.',
'The problem is actually very general and applies to any region content that is wider',
'than the page.',
'</p>',
'<p>The root cause is that the APEX Universal Theme page is optimized for ',
'vertical scrolling. All the UT page templates work this way. It is part of the',
'responsive design. But not all web pages are intended to be viewed on a phone.',
'If you have a report with 50 or so columns and hundreds of rows you probably ',
'intend it to be viewed on a desktop screen. UT does not provide a page template',
'for this.',
'</p>',
'<p>This page shows a solution to the problem using the standard UT page template.',
'See the Split Grid and Form Multi-edit page for an example that uses ',
'custom page template Fit to Window. The IG defaults of scroll pagination and',
'heading fixed to page are designed to work well with the UT intention of only',
'vertical scrolling. If you have a region that is wider and taller than the browser',
'window or you have multiple regions either side by side or one on top of the other',
'and the regions need to scroll either horzontally or vertically or both then ',
'the browser window should not scroll, all regions should fit on the page, and',
'each of the regions should have their own scrollbars. APEX and UT do not make ',
'this automatic but it is possible.</p>',
'<p>This example uses a static Notes region and an Interactive Grid but the ',
'technique is easily adapted to other region types and also applies to editable IG',
'regions.</p>',
'<ul>',
'<li>If the region to scroll supports sticky headers or footers turn them off.',
'For IG this means set header fixed to region and give it a reasonably small height.</li>',
'<li>Use the Standard page template and make some minor CSS changes to get it ready',
'for not scrolling. See the page inline CSS attribute. You may want to remove ',
'padding, get rid of the body content min-height and hide the footer back to top link.',
'You could also create your own custom page template for example if you didn''t want',
'to have any footer.</li>',
'<li>The remaining step and the part that needs to be customized for each use case is',
'to resize all the regions so they fit exactly on the page so the browser window',
'never has a scroll bar. See the code in the Execute when Page Loads attribute.',
'The width will generally take care of itself. Start with the window height and',
'subtract off all the regions with a fixed height as well as the page header.',
'Then apportion the remaining height to the variable sized regions. Set the height',
'of the region and/or widget inside the region. If the region widget has a',
'resize method you may need to call it. Getting the height just right can take',
'some investigation to find some padding, border or margin somewhere on the page',
'that is causing a scrollbar on the window or extra blank space.',
'You need to use the apexwindowresized event to redo the calculation any time',
'the window size changes.',
'</li>',
'</ul>',
'</p> ',
'<p>Customizations:<br>',
'See the page attributes Inline CSS and Execute when Page Loads. The region ',
'template options didn''t have a small enough height for the notes region so',
'I added i-h140 to the region CSS classes.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'You need to consider what happens if the page does go responsive because',
'UT changes how the page layout grid is layed out and how region height is determined',
'for small screens.<br>',
'The UT classes and ids such as t-Header and t_Body_content_offset and API',
'apex.util.setOuterHeight are not documented.',
'</p>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
