wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(36339109093646814278)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Some people have wanted to use the Rich Text Editor item in IG columns ',
'(see <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/message/14605307#14605307">here</a> for example).</p>',
'',
'<p>This page shows a work around that allows a column to use a Rich Text Editor.',
'It uses the Custom Popup plug-in for three columns. It is used to pick the Manager using ',
'an IG region in a popup, enter compensation in a dialog and to edit notes',
'in a rich text editor in a dialog. The plug-in can be configured to open',
'with a button or on focus. Play around with the Has Button and Display Under Field',
'attributes. It works with either inline popups or inline dialogs. ',
'It can be used for normal page items as well. There is a demo/test',
'page for the Custom Popup plug-in <a href="f?p=&APP_ID.:530:&SESSION.">here</a>.</p>',
'',
'<p>Demonstrates:<p>',
'<ul>',
'<li>A general purpose item plug-in called Custom Popup that can be used to get a value from any inline modal dialog.',
'This plug-in is an example of an item plug-in designed to work as a column or page item.</li>',
'<li>How to put a Rich Text Editor in an inline modal dialog region. (See DA notes dlg add methods.)</li>',
'<li>How to put an Interactive Grid in an inline modal dialog/popup region. (This got easier in 18.2)</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>Customizations:<br>',
'The Custom Popup column item type is used for the MGR, SAL, and NOTES columns.',
'The IG used to select a manager is configured to minimize functionality so that',
'it is focused on filtering and selecting. Most of the interesting stuff is in ',
'the inline dialog and inline popup regions and their many Dynamic Actions.',
'Remember to use the correct widget depending on if',
'it is a dialog or popup. For example use event popupopen or dialogopen.',
'The SAL Custom Popup demonstrates how the plug-in supports multiple inputs and outputs.',
'There are also a few inline CSS styles for the inline regions.',
'There is a disabled region Test Custom Popup that shows how the plug-in can',
'be used for page items. See the Custom Popup plug-in defintion in shared components',
'and read the help for the various Custom Popup attributes. It is possible for ',
'more than one Custom Popup item to use the same inline region.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'The math in the Compensation dialog probably needs fine tuning.<br>',
'This is-readonly class on the COMM column doesn''t keep it from being edited in single row view.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
