wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(32334453922033002564)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>This page demonstrates two things. 1) How to put an Interactive Grid into',
'an Inline Dialog region. 2) How to disassociate the detail region from the ',
'master so that the detail model instance is only set on demand.',
'It also demonstrates how to deal with the IG master detail limitation where ',
'it is not clear which detials have been edited and if there is a validation',
'error in any of the detail record edits the user has no idea which one it is.',
'The links in the validation message area only work if the correct detail record',
'is already showing.',
'There is code on this page to show with colors and tooltips which ',
'master records have edits or errors in detail records.',
'</p>',
'<p>Steps for adding an Interactive Grid to an inline dialog or popup region. ',
'(Note: prior to 18.2 there were a number of bugs that had to be worked around',
'in order to put an IG in an inline dialog.)',
'<ul>',
'<li>Create a region in the Inline Dialogs possition. The region template should',
'be Inline Dialog or Inline Popup (Prior to 19.1 you could <a target="_blank" href="http://hardlikesoftware.com/weblog/2018/04/20/apex-inline-popup-region/">create Inline Popup</a>).',
'The IG can be the inline region or it can be a sub region. Give the region ',
'a static id.</li>',
'<li>On the IG region set Heading: Fixed To = Region because the sticky headers',
'and footer make no sense in a dialog; they only apply to the scrollable main page.',
'Set the desired region height and check the Inline Dialog template option Auto Height ',
'or, even better, give it a reasonable small height such as 200 and adjust',
'the height to fit the dialog as described in a later step.',
'Set Lazy Loading to Yes because there is no point in loading data until it will',
'be seen.</li>',
'<li>If the IG is in a sub region of the dialog use template Standard and',
'configure template options to remove body padding, remove borders, header hidden,',
'and set all margins to none. This still leaves padding in the dialog content.',
'A region like IG should fill the dialog. Use the Inline region Remove Body Padding',
'template option for this.</li>',
'<li>To make the IG region resize to fit the dialog add a dynamic action on the',
'custom events "dialogresizestop dialogopen" See the code in DA "resize emp ig".</li>',
unistr('<li>If the dialog doesn\2019t contain an item that would automatically take focus'),
'then it is a good idea to explicitly set focus. So for an IG create a DA on ',
'custom event dialogopen. See the code in DA "focus on emp open".</li>',
'<li>If the IG is editable you probably want to remove the Save button from the toolbar.',
'When the edits are saved depends on the use case. You may want to save ',
'when the dialog closes or perhaps when the page is submitted or in the case',
'of master detail when the master region is saved. Here are two possible use cases:',
'1) Letting the master do the save. That is what this page demonstrates. ',
'2) Force save or cancel changes to leave the dialog. See page Master Detail Dialog (save).</li>',
'</ul>',
'</p>',
'<p>Customizations:<br>',
'See page inline CSS and Function and Global Variable Declaration. See JavaScript Initialization Code',
'for dept and emp IGs. See the OPEN_DETAIL column and all the dynamic actions.',
'Note the use of new API apex.theme.openRegion and DA Close Region.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'IG master detail should have a way to navigate to the correct detail record(s)',
'that have errors.<br>',
'Beware bug 27989333 INTERACTIVE GRID MASTER DETAIL ERROR WHEN SAVE NEW MASTER WITH DETAILS,',
'which prevents you from creating a new master record and adding detail records to it',
'at the same time.',
'The workaround is to remove the Save button from the master region and instead ',
'submit the page. In this case I did not want to submit the page.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
