wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(32334731896013362495)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--noPadding:t-Region--removeHeader js-removeLandmark:t-Region--noBorder:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108658789039181378)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>20
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>This page demonstrates how to make interactive grid not load and render any data until',
'the tab it is in is activated. When an IG is configured to lazy load it ',
'doesn''t include any data in the page but instead uses ajax to request data',
'once the page is ready in the browser. In addition it will not request data',
'while it is not visible. This is something specific to',
'interactive grid. Hopefully in the future more APEX regions will behave this way.',
'Use the JavaScript console or Network tab to observe when the ajax requests',
'happen. Compare any of the IG views with the Chart tab. (Starting in 19.1 ',
'the lazy loading when not visible works for IG chart, icon, and detail views.)',
'</p>',
'<p>This not loading until visible works automatically with collapsible region templates',
'and starting in 18.2 with inline dialogs.',
'The trouble with region display selector tabs is that all tabs are visible',
'for a brief moment when the page loads so at initialization time the IG is not',
'invisible and will load and render the data. For background see',
'<a href="http://hardlikesoftware.com/weblog/2017/11/07/visibility-and-size-managed-components/" target="_blank">this blog</a>.</p>',
'<p>The solution is to use a css rule to make the tabs initially invisible',
'and to force the initially visible tab to notifiy that it is active.',
'See the code in page attribute Execute when Page Loads and Inline CSS.',
'Note: If you have any tabs with components that don''t initialize correctly when',
'invisible you have more work to do. See above linked blog.',
'</p>',
'<p>The one problem with this page is that the three IGs share the same',
'document scroll offset. So as you move from one tab to another the ',
'scroll offset can shift. This may not be a problem if none of the IGs contain',
'many rows. You could add complex logic to try to save and restore',
'the scroll offset for each tab or you could switch to Pagination Type Page.',
'Another, in my opinion better, solution is to take the advice given on page',
'"Wide Report"</p>',
'<p style="margin-left: 2em;">"If you have ... multiple regions either side by side or one on top of the other and the regions need to scroll either horzontally or vertically or both then the browser window should not scroll, all regions should fit on'
||' the page, and each of the regions should have their own scrollbars."',
'</p>',
'<p>See page Lazy Tabs (fit page) for a demonstration where each tab has its own scrollbar.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
