wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(4228286688862380153)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_name=>'notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108658789039181378)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>20
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_04'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>This page is an example of what can be done with a model. ',
'Interactive Grid provides a model layer that interacts with the sever',
'to fetch records and save changes. This can be leveraged without using any of',
'the IG region UI. Ideally there would be a region type that creates a raw model',
'from data and a corresponding DML process. It would not be hard to create such',
'a model region but currently the Interactive Grid - Automatic Row Processing (DML) process',
'is hard coded to only work with IG regions and duplicating its functionality is not',
'really possible.</p>',
'<p>The idea for this example came from this <a target="_blank" href="https://community.oracle.com/thread/4172540">forum question</a>.',
'This page lets you edit the details of multiple employees at the same time each in their ',
'own tab. This UI pattern is not very common on the web but it is common ',
'for desktop apps to provide a tabbed "document" style editing UI.',
'</p>',
'<p>Demonstrates:</p>',
'<ul>',
'<li>Creating a hidden minimal editable IG region and detaching the model from the view',
'so the model can be used for any purpose. The model including its columns and assoication',
'with a database table is all declarativly configured with the IG region. Saving changes',
'is handled by the normal IG automatic DML Process.</li>',
'<li>Creating a jQuery UI Tabs region template. Extending tabs to support',
'adding and removing tabs. Also allow tabs to be reordered with touch support.',
'Used jQuery UI Tabs rather than APEX RDS or Tabs Container (aTabs widget) because',
'it is documented and it may not even be possible to support add and remove with aTabs.',
'This shows how easy it is to use jQuery UI Tabs in an APEX app. jQuery tabs and',
'aTabs have different but overlaping functionality; pick based on what you need.</li>',
'<li>Create new form elements based on a template form made up of real APEX page items.',
'This is a bit of a hack but can be made to work especially for basic item types.',
'The alternative is to do client side template processing and instanciate ',
'widgets as needed. Could use apex.util.applyTemplate or bring in a 3rd party',
'template library but I think this cloning with fix up is easier; at least in this case.</li>',
'<li>Simple data binding with the APEX model layer. This is very basic and I hope',
'in the future it is much easier and/or automatic/declarative.</li>',
'<li>This is yet another page that resizes to fit the window.</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>Areas for improvement:<br>',
'Client side validation, better validation error handling, ability to save a single tab.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
