wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(32026801975896420829)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_name=>'notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--noPadding:t-Region--hideHeader:t-Region--noBorder:t-Region--scrollBody:margin-top-none:margin-bottom-none'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108658789039181378)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>20
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Sometimes Interactive Grid has more features than you need. One way to deal with this',
'is to turn off, disable, or customize away what you don''t want.',
'Page <a href="f?p=&APP_ID.:20:&SESSION.">IG Cards</a> is a good example of this approach.',
'Another option is to create a plug-in that utilizes the underlying widgets to do',
'exactly what you want and no more. This page demonstrates the Simple Grid plug-in.',
'Simple Grid is a region plug-in built around the APEX grid widget. The grid widget',
'and model are now fairly well documented enabling the creation of custom plug-ins',
'such as this. This plug-in also uses the APEX_EXEC API to',
'fetch the data so it should work with web sources and remote databases.</p>',
'<p>One thing that people often ask for is to support source type ',
'PL/SQL Function Body returning SQL Query with Interactive Report and',
'Interactive Grid just like in Classic Reports. Even now that it is supported for',
'Interactive Report (and if it is ever supported for Interactive Grid) it has',
'the restriction that the SQL statement returned must always have the same columns.',
'For various reasons people have wanted to do what Classic reports can do and ',
'have different columns in the report. The reason the Interactive regions can''t',
'support this is because of saved reports, which rely on knowledge about the columns.',
'The Simple Grid has no saved reports and so it was possible (not easy) to support',
'dynamic columns. See the Table Browser tab. Note that column state (order, show, width, and freeze)',
'is persisted for the browser session per table. The result is a single region',
'that can report on various tables while leveraging the features of grid widget such',
'as scroll paging, selection, and frozen columns.</p>',
'<p>Demonstrates:<br>',
'Creating a region plug-in that uses the grid widget and the APEX_EXEC API.',
'Study the Simple Grid plug-in source PL/SQL and JavaScript files carefully. ',
'Simple Grid is probably not generally useful as is. Use it as a starting point',
'for creating a region that does just what you want. There are many design',
'choices that could be made differently and areas to improve. For example ',
'filtering UI could be made a part of the plug-in rather than just exposing an',
'API that allows custom UI for filtering. Areas to improve include column link ',
'options, and more filtering capabilities. Note: a similar region plug-in',
'could be created for the tableModelView widget to make a Simple Icon or Detail',
'report region.</p>',
'<p>Play around with the region attributes of the Simple Grid and Data regions.',
'See Execute when Page Loads page attribute for tab panel resize logic ',
'(this is similar to the Lazy Tabs fit page example but more complicated because of the tab contents),',
'how the list of columns to filter is generated when the Simple Grid tab is ',
'activated (have to wait unitl the grid is initialized), and how the tableData',
'region is updated when the table changes (this uses apex.util.debounce to avoid',
'updating the grid if the table select list changes rapidly using keyboard arrows).',
'Simple Grid doesn''t have built in UI for filtering but it does support filtering.',
'This lets you create any kind of UI that you like for the user to enter filters.',
'The inline filter popup region is just an example of what can be done. ',
'See that region and the related dynamic actions for how it works.</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
