wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(33176550139835857582)
,p_plug_name=>'Notes'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-useLocalStorage:is-collapsed:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(35108653483362181373)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_include_in_reg_disp_sel_yn=>'Y'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>File this under things that should be easy but are not. In fact remembering ',
'what results page you are on should be automatic like it is with Interactive Reports.',
'The use case is that you are using Pagination Type = Page and you have one or more',
'links that take you to other pages and when you return to this page you want the',
'results to be showing the same page. In addition since IG supports selection',
'probably the same records should be selected. In theory it should be possible',
'to manually code a workaround but as I found out it is complicated. To remember ',
'the page requires 3 things:',
'</p>',
'<ol>',
'<li>Getting the current IG page number before leaving the page. There is no API ',
'to get the current page but there is an event when the page changes.',
'If the rows per page is set to Auto (the default) the number of rows depends',
'on the window or region size and if the size changes between the time the page',
'is retrieved and restored the page could be completely different.',
'</li>',
'<li>Saving the current IG page number somewhere. With interactive report the server',
'remembers the page/record offset but because the IG uses a client side model',
'the current page need not be the last page of results requested from the server.',
'This doesn''t really mater for a client side workaround.',
'</li>',
'<li>Restoring the IG results page when returning to the page. This needs to be',
'done conditionally because there are cases where you want to return to the',
'first page. This is what the Reset Pagination (RP) URL field is for.',
'There is the gotoPage API to go to a specific page but it only works if the',
'Show Total Row Count attribute is On/Yes.',
'</li>',
'</ol>',
'<p>The solution should be robust and work no mater if using grid, icon, or ',
'detail views. It should work no matter the IG settings such as Show Total Row Count',
'or Lazy Loading. It should be efficient and not make more ajax requests than it needs.',
'Unlike IR, IG keeps separate sort order for icon and detail views because they',
'have a separate model. It makes sense that they should have separate page ',
'and selection as well.',
'</p>',
'<p>Although there is no API to get the current page the pagechange event',
'will give you the current offset and count. From this you can calculate the page number if needed.',
'Keep in mind that the page is zero based. The ideal place to remember the',
'current page is in browser session storage. It also makes sense to use',
'the RP URL field to control if pagination should be reset or not.',
'If you click on the Remember Page on side navigation the pagination will be reset.',
'Setting the page turned out to be difficult to do robustly and efficiently.',
'The gotoPage method is not too useful because the page size could change if rows per',
'page is set to auto and because the model is going to fetch starting from offset 0',
'and you have to wait until that completes before calling gotoPage in many cases.',
'</p>',
'<p>Customizations:<br>',
'Remembering the selection requires that Select First Row is false/off.<br>',
'Most of the code for this example is in page attribute Function and Global Variable Declaration.',
'Some of that code is called from Execute when Page Loads. The only Advanced ',
'JavaScript Initialization code is to turn off single row mode because it complicated things.<br>',
'Note: There is an Interactive Report on this page that is excluded. I was using',
'it to compare functionality.<br>',
'The need to return to a specific page can be partially avoided if you use ',
'modal APEX dialog pages and/or use scroll paging. With scroll paging there is a ',
'desire to remember the scroll offset but that is an example for another day.',
'<br>Issues:<br>',
'I consider this a work in progress. It needs much more testing. For example',
'it tries to be general and work for any IGs on the page but so far I have only tested',
'with the one. Restoring the selection seems to need more work.',
'It should probably be more robust for example by making sure that the',
'IG is using pagination Type = Page. It does use internal undocumented details.',
'Study the code and comments well.<br>',
'Remebering the page and possibly the selection should be a built-in feature.<br>',
'In a case like this it is better to set (go to) the offset rather than the page.<br>',
'It may make sense to have an API to get the current page/offset.<br>',
'There needs to be a way to set the initial offset during initialization and the model',
'can''t assume that it is always going to start with offset 0.<br>',
'The DA Event "Page Change [Interactive Grid]" should apply to the IG as a whole but',
'currently only applies to the grid view. So need to use a custom event',
'"gridpagechange tablemodelviewpagechange" to cover both events.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
